"""Editorial question maps for time and reality, and intellectual puzzles."""

from review_angle_plans import audit, revise_domain


TIME = """history_origins|How a Time Concept Developed|Which question led a named thinker or scientist to redefine time?|Read the original text and distinguish its scientific and philosophical claims.
famous_examples|A Famous Time Experiment|What did one well-known clock comparison actually measure?|Use the published method, uncertainty, and interpretation rather than an analogy alone.
hidden_stories|The People Behind Timekeeping|Whose measurement, calibration, or coordination work made a time standard possible?|Use dated laboratory and institutional records with attributed contributions.
beginner_explainers|Clock Time, Experienced Time, and Spacetime|Which meaning of time is at issue in one familiar question?|Define the measurement, subjective report, or philosophical thesis separately.
advanced_concepts|Simultaneity Under Scrutiny|How does one physical framework define whether distant events are simultaneous?|Explain the stated frame and assumptions through an authoritative derivation.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|What Remains Open About Time?|Which specific time-related question is not settled by a cited experiment?|Distinguish empirical uncertainty, conceptual dispute, and speculative proposal.
technology_innovation|A More Precise Clock|What improved when one timekeeping method replaced an earlier one?|Compare accuracy, stability, application, and uncertainty in original records.
people_personalities|A Thinker's View of Time|Which assumptions drove one named account of temporal passage?|Reconstruct a primary argument and a serious objection.
major_events|A Change in Time Standards|What problem led an institution to revise a time standard?|Trace dated decisions, measurement evidence, and implementation.
how_it_works|How a Time Standard Is Realized|How does a defined physical measurement become a shared time scale?|Use metrology documents and separate unit definition from practical realization.
rise_fall|A Theory of Time in Debate|Why did one account gain or lose support among relevant researchers?|Compare original claims, objections, experiments, and limits of consensus measures.
then_vs_now|Timekeeping Across Two Eras|How did precision and coordination change for a specified use?|Compare the same measurement task and error metric at two dates.
future_developments|An Open Question in Time Research|What future observation could discriminate two named proposals?|State predictions, measurement sensitivity, and conditions for a useful test.
myths_vs_facts|Checking a Time-Travel Claim|Does a popular claim follow from the theory or experiment it cites?|Trace the original source and mark the gap between measured effect and fiction.
documentary_stories|One Time Experiment Through Its Records|How did a specific study move from proposal to result and interpretation?|Build a dated timeline of apparatus, data, paper, and subsequent checks.
assumption_inventory|What a Time Claim Assumes|Which definitions and physical assumptions support one conclusion?|List frame, clock, event, and inferential steps before evaluating the claim.
readiness_check|From Clock Prototype to Standard|What evidence supports wider use of a new timekeeping technique?|Compare repeatability, calibration, uncertainty, infrastructure, and independent labs.
physical_limits|Limits of a Proposed Time Machine|Which established physical constraints challenge a specific fictional or theoretical device?|State the model and its assumptions without presenting speculative mechanisms as engineering plans.
governance_choice|Who Defines Civil Time?|Which institutions decide a civil time rule in one jurisdiction?|Read current official standards and decision records; separate politics from physics.
unequal_futures|Who Benefits From Precision Time?|Which users can access precise timing, and who bears infrastructure costs?|Compare named applications, service access, resilience, and cost.
scenario_pair|Two Rules for Coordinating Time|What changes under two proposed timekeeping policies?|Hold the use case constant and compare transition cost, error, and affected users.
failure_to_launch|A Timekeeping Proposal That Stalled|Why did one proposed clock or calendar reform fail to spread?|Compare technical merit with governance, compatibility, and public use.
unintended_effect|A Timing Change's Side Effects|Which downstream systems were affected by one dated time-rule change?|Trace public implementation and incident records without operational vulnerabilities.
social_adaptation|Living With a Time Convention|How did one community adapt to a change in clock or calendar practice?|Use dated local records and attributed accounts rather than assuming uniform experience.
ethical_boundary|Who Controls Time Data?|What privacy or fairness concerns arise from one high-resolution timing application?|Define data, users, purpose, retention, and affected groups.
signal_vs_hype|A Claim of New Physics|Does one apparent time anomaly survive calibration and replication?|Read original measurements, uncertainties, independent checks, and corrections.
reversible_steps|Testing a Time Policy|What limited trial could reveal the effects of a proposed timing change?|Specify users, measurements, oversight, rollback, and confounders.
field_world_rule|Rules in a Time Fiction|Which rules about memory, causality, and clocks govern one fictional world?|Use the work's explicit scenes and distinguish internal consistency from physics.
field_plausibility_boundary|Where Fiction Leaves Evidence|Which elements of a time story rest on measured physics and which are invented?|Compare cited physical results with the story's added premises.
field_point_of_view|Who Experiences the Timeline?|How does viewpoint change the audience's understanding of sequence?|Trace scenes and narrator knowledge in one work without treating narrative order as physical time.
field_ethical_consequence|Changing the Past as a Moral Problem|Which obligations follow within one fictional time-travel rule?|Analyze consequences for named characters and the work's own constraints.
field_adaptation_choice|A Time Story Across Media|How did an adaptation represent sequence differently from its source?|Compare original and adaptation scenes, constraints, and audience comprehension."""


PUZZLES = """history_origins|The Earliest Trace of a Puzzle|Where does a named puzzle first appear in the surviving record?|Compare dated publications, variants, and uncertain attributions.
famous_examples|A Classic Puzzle Reexamined|What makes one famous puzzle surprising, and what exactly is its solution?|State rules, prove the result, and compare common mistaken approaches.
hidden_stories|Creators Behind a Puzzle|Whose design, translation, testing, or community contribution went uncredited?|Trace publication and testimony while respecting authorship claims.
beginner_explainers|How to Read a Puzzle|Which facts are given, which are rules, and what counts as a solution?|Work through one small example with a checkable answer.
advanced_concepts|Why a Puzzle Has One Answer|How can uniqueness be established for a defined logic puzzle?|Show a proof or exhaustive reproducible check and note assumptions.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|A Genuine Open Problem|Is a claimed unsolved puzzle open to everyone or only under a particular rule set?|Verify the formal statement, prior work, and current status before production.
technology_innovation|A Solver as a Test Tool|What can a computer search establish about one finite puzzle?|Compare code, search space, independent verification, and proof limits.
people_personalities|A Puzzle Maker's Design Choice|Why did a named creator set one constraint or clue?|Use drafts, interviews, publication records, and tested effects.
major_events|A Competition Changes Puzzle Culture|What changed after one documented tournament, publication, or release?|Compare participation, rules, formats, and community response.
how_it_works|From Rules to Deduction|How does a valid inference narrow possibilities in one puzzle?|Show each premise and conclusion so the audience can check the reasoning.
rise_fall|A Puzzle Format's Popularity|Why did one format spread or fade?|Compare distribution, technology, communities, and rule changes across dates.
then_vs_now|A Puzzle Across Editions|How did rules, layout, difficulty, or audience change?|Compare original and later editions with equivalent criteria.
future_developments|A New Puzzle Variant|What does a proposed rule change add to the solution space?|Test examples, solvability, uniqueness, and accessibility before making claims.
myths_vs_facts|A Puzzle Attribution Checked|Is a famous origin or inventor story supported by dated evidence?|Trace earliest printed version and later retellings.
documentary_stories|One Puzzle's Publication Trail|How did an idea become a widely solved puzzle?|Build a dated record of draft, editor, release, variants, and reception.
creative_brief|The Designer's Puzzle Goal|Which experience or insight did one puzzle aim to create?|Compare brief, prototype, final rules, and solver feedback.
materials_and_tools|Physical and Digital Puzzle Forms|How do pieces, print layout, or interface constrain one puzzle?|Study one edition's materials, legibility, and alternative formats.
process_breakdown|How a Puzzle Was Constructed|What revisions made one puzzle valid and engaging?|Use designer notes, solver testing, and uniqueness checks.
composition_choice|Ordering Clues and Information|How did clue order affect difficulty without changing the solution?|Compare equivalent versions and documented solver behavior.
collaborative_authorship|Who Made the Final Puzzle?|How did constructor, editor, test solvers, and publisher share decisions?|Check credits, correspondence, and revision history.
adaptation_across_media|A Puzzle Changes Medium|What changes when a paper puzzle becomes an app or audio experience?|Compare rules, feedback, interaction, and accessibility.
audience_reception|How Solvers Responded|Which parts of one puzzle caused delight, confusion, or exclusion?|Use documented feedback with sample limits, not anecdotes as universal outcomes.
cultural_context|A Puzzle's Required Knowledge|Which cultural references or conventions must a solver know?|Identify assumptions and compare audiences without ranking their intelligence.
preservation_restoration|Keeping an Old Puzzle Playable|What must be preserved when restoring a historical puzzle?|Compare original rules, materials, missing pieces, and explanatory additions.
rights_and_attribution|Crediting a Puzzle's Source|Who owns or is credited for one puzzle edition or adaptation?|Check dates, licenses, contracts, and jurisdiction before reuse.
style_comparison|Two Puzzles, One Mechanic|How do two designers use the same rule to create different experiences?|Compare equivalent constraints, clue density, and solver paths.
creative_failure|A Puzzle That Failed in Testing|Why did solvers find one design ambiguous, trivial, or inaccessible?|Compare intended solution with playtest evidence and revisions.
field_rules_design|A Rule That Changes Everything|How does one rule alter the valid solutions of a puzzle?|State both rule sets and prove or enumerate the differences.
field_player_strategy|A Checkable Solving Method|Which logical method works for a defined puzzle class?|Demonstrate it on one example and distinguish a heuristic from proof.
field_difficulty_curve|Measuring Difficulty|Which measures explain why one puzzle feels harder than another?|Compare solver populations, time, error, hint use, and rule familiarity.
field_community_norms|Hints and Fair Play|How does one puzzle community define acceptable hints or outside tools?|Use published rules and attributed participant views, avoiding a universal standard.
field_accessibility_design|More Ways to Solve|Which visual, motor, language, or cognitive barriers affect one puzzle?|Test alternative representations with affected solvers and preserve the core logic."""


if __name__ == "__main__":
    revise_domain("055", "055_time_reality", TIME,
                  "Time and reality through measurement, relativity, philosophical arguments, civil coordination, and clearly labeled fictional rules.",
                  "primary physics papers and measurement records, BIPM and national-metrology standards, original philosophical texts, official civil-time decisions, and cited creative works",
                  "Distinguish measured time effects, philosophical interpretations, subjective reports, policy conventions, and fiction. State frame, definition, date, uncertainty, and source; never present speculative time travel as established physics.")
    revise_domain("056", "056_puzzles_intellectual_mysteries", PUZZLES,
                  "Puzzles and intellectual mysteries through precise rules, proofs, design choices, publication history, solving experience, and accessibility.",
                  "original puzzle publications and editions, designer notes, formal proofs or reproducible solver checks, competition rules, playtest evidence, and accessibility feedback",
                  "State the exact rule set and edition. Verify uniqueness and open-problem status, credit creators and adaptations, and distinguish a solution, heuristic, and unsupported claim.")
    rows = audit()
    print(f"Plans: {len(rows)}; reviewed question designs: {sum(r['status'] == 'editorial_question_reviewed' for r in rows)}")
